        <name>read_view</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The read view of this transaction. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When a transaction is started, it is set to the &quot;read committed&quot; state, or actually, &quot;read prepared&quot; state, in other words, all changes of all prepared transactions are visible to this transaction. Upon a conflict, the transaction&apos;s read view is changed: it begins to point to the last state of the database before the conflicting change. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
